course: dictionary
lesson: 7130
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pencil is a thin stick of wood with a core of grey graphite inside, used for writing and drawing. Scientists call that core graphite, not lead, even though people often say the «lead» in a pencil.
explain: Look at the context to see which meaning fits. «Anna has 18 pencils and shares them equally among 2 friends» is about things you can count. «Sharpen your pencil» is about the tool you write with.
explain: Pencil can also be a verb. «I will pencil the trip in for next Friday» means write it down for now, maybe to change later. Ask: what would fit here? If pen would fit and the plan is final, the meaning is different; pencil means you may change it later.
fact: A pencil is a thin stick of wood with graphite inside, for writing and drawing.
fact: A coloured pencil is a pencil for drawing in colours.
fact: To pencil something in means to write it down for now, maybe to change later.
fact: «If 6 of those 24 pencils are given away, 24 − 6 = 18 are left.»
fact: A pencil is made of baked graphite and clay, sandwiched between two slats of cedar wood, glued, cut and painted.
exercise: «At the end of a lesson, put books, pencils and papers back where they belong.» What is a pencil in this sentence? | A wax crayon for colouring | *A thin stick of wood with graphite inside, for writing | A pencil case full of pens | A rubber for rubbing out
exercise: Mia says, «I will pencil the party in my diary.» What does pencil mean here? | To sharpen a stick of wood | To draw a picture of a party | To buy a new diary | *To write it down for now, maybe to change later
exercise: «If 6 of those 24 pencils are given away, how many are left?» | 30 | 6 | *18 | 24
test: «Coloured pencil» means what? | *A pencil for drawing in colours | A stick of graphite for writing in grey only | A type of paint brush | A rubber that smells of fruit
test: Which is true about the «lead» in a pencil? | It is a kind of paint | *It is graphite, not real lead | It is made of wax and clay | It is real lead that is very heavy
exam: Which sentence uses pencil as a verb? | There are 18 pencils in the box | *I will pencil the trip in for next Friday, maybe to change later | I sharpened my pencil before class | I drew a cat with a red pencil
